<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06W6">Example <span data-tag="06W6">9.6.6.5</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a locally Kan simplicial category containing morphisms $f: A \rightarrow B$ and $g: X \rightarrow Y$. Then $f$ is left orthogonal to $g$ in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ if and only if the diagram of Kan complexes </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(B,X)_{\bullet } \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,X)_{\bullet } \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( B, Y)_{\bullet } \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A, Y)_{\bullet } } \]
</div>
<p> is a homotopy pullback square. See Proposition <a data-tag="03N7" href="/tag/03N7">8.3.6.2</a> and Example <a data-tag="03G5" href="/tag/03G5">7.6.3.2</a>. </p>
</article>
